===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|wynne}}, {{m|en|winne}}, {{m|enm|wenne}}, {{m|enm|wunne}}, {{m|enm|wyn}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wynn|t=joy, pleasure}} (runes were named using words beginning with their sound), from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wunnju}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wunjō}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wn̥h₁yeh₂}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*wenh₁-|t=desire, wish, love}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/wɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-win.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-win.wav|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪn|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|win|winne|;|when<aa:with both the <<wine-whine>> and <<pin-pen>>>}}

===Noun===
[[Image:Wynn.png|right|Wynn]]
{{en-noun}}

# {{topics|en|Latin letter names|Runic letter names}} A letter of the Old English alphabet, [[ƿ]], borrowed from the [[futhark]] and used to represent the sound of ''w''; replaced in Middle English times by the digraph ''uu'', which later developed into the letter [[w]].

